{
  "id": "ex-post-facto-evaluation",
  "term": "ex post facto evaluation",
  "definition": "An ex post facto evaluation is an assessment carried out after a program or intervention has already occurred, using existing differences between people or groups to compare outcomes rather than assigning conditions in advance. In the source, it refers to a quasi-experimental, after-the-fact comparison of users and non-users, which can show associations but may not support causal conclusions.",
